CLAUDE.md:51:There is no linter config; `tests/` (pytest, 171 tests, ~3 min, `python -m pytest tests -q` in the xRIR env) covers the exp_03 tools (`tools/yaw_rotation.py`, `tools/reference_manifest.py`, `tools/paired_stats.py`, `tools/per_sample_metrics.py`, `eval_yaw_rotation.py`, `tools/summarize_yaw.py`). The original eval scripts run `batch_size=1` with `shuffle=True` over the whole test split and print running averages; use `eval_xRIR_backbone.py` (deterministic order, `--max-samples`, JSON summary, identical metric code) for anything that needs to be compared or bounded. Full-split eval takes about an hour per split at ~1.7 samples/s; training is ~1.4 s/iter at batch 32 with TF32 (~3.6 h/epoch on 296k samples), so budget accordingly and rely on `best.pth` / `last.pth` + `--resume`.
