CLAUDE.md:77:**Sim-to-real** (`sim_to_real/`): two-stage fine-tuning on Hearing-Anything-Anywhere (HAA) rooms. The original scripts (`finetune_all_rooms.py`, `finetune_classroom.py`, `eval_classroom.py`, `haa_*_dataset.py`) carry `/pscratch/...` placeholders and select checkpoints on the test split; keep them as reference only. The runnable pipeline is the parallel set: `prepare_haa.py` (builds `~/data_cache/HAA_xrir/<room>/` from `/media/diskstation/yixunhu/HAA_processed`, normalizing each room by the max amplitude of its 12 DiffRIR training RIRs), `haa_dataset.py` (same tuple as `xRIR_Dataset`; speaker = model "receiver", mics = "sources"; deterministic eval references via `eval_seed`), `finetune_haa.py` (repo recipe, `--backbone`, selection on the DiffRIR validation split), `eval_haa.py` (Table-2 metrics on full 9600-sample waveforms, T60 skipped for `dampened_room`, per-sample JSON), `run_haa_pipeline.sh` (one GPU queue of `<init>:<seed>` jobs into `ckpt/sim2real/`), `summarize_haa.py`. Known asset bugs: the released `sim_to_real/depth_map/complex_room.npy` is byte-identical to `hallway.npy`, and `dampened_room.npy` is misaligned with the pose frame, so the cache uses the HAA_processed renders for those two rooms (`depth_default` in each `meta.json`; `--depth-variant repo` reproduces the released assets). Result (exp_02, 2026-09-06, canonical `ckpt/sim2real/stats.json`): after fine-tuning, the SimpleViT control beats CylindricalViT on 6/11 room×metric cells (hallway by 43–81 %) and loses none; the released checkpoint does not reproduce Table 2 on hallway/complex under this protocol while our control does on EDT. `summarize_haa.py` enforces a strict completeness gate (exact DiffRIR indices, protocol meta, stage `args.json` seed/init/depth_variant) and writes hash-bound `--json`/`--summary` artefacts that the results page consumes.
CLAUDE.md:89:Current experiment (on `main`): test whether swapping SimpleViT for CylindricalViT improves few-shot RIR prediction. The paper's Table 1 (xRIR K=8: seen EDT 0.038 s / C50 0.940 dB / T60 8.13 %, unseen 0.055 / 1.457 / ~10 %) was reproduced on 2026-09-04 with the released checkpoints via `eval_unseen.py` / `eval_seen.py`: seen 0.039 / 1.03 / 7.27, unseen 0.055 / 1.36 / 9.69 (full splits; see `ckpt/baseline_reproduction.json`). Reference selection is random, so expect run-to-run noise of that size. The comparison trains `--backbone cylindrical` and a same-budget `--backbone simple` control with identical flags (`ckpt/xRIR_cyl_8_shot`, `ckpt/xRIR_simple_8_shot`; `train.log`, `history.jsonl`, `args.json` inside each), because the released checkpoints' training budget is unknown. The paper text says a 6-layer ViT; the code and checkpoints use `depth=12`. Result (2026-09-05, canonical `ckpt/backbone_comparison_stats.json` / `summary.txt`): averaged over epochs 5-12 on the unseen split, CylindricalViT beats the same-budget SimpleViT control on EDT (-3.7%, all 8 epochs), the objective (-1.2%) and log-STFT MSE (-1.3%) with query-level CIs excluding 0 (inference about this fixed split); with the 17 rooms as bootstrap unit every interval includes 0; C50/T60 no detected difference. Caveat: evaluation references were NOT identical across models (loader seed drawn after model construction) and Griffin-Lim phases were unseeded; the paired re-evaluation is exp_03's k=0 gate. Per-epoch files: `ckpt/xRIR_{cyl,simple}_8_shot/{epoch_NN.pth, per_sample_unseen_epochNN.json, eval_unseen_epochNN.json}`.
CLAUDE.md:91:exp_03 (yaw rotation, 2026-09-06, SOP-native, record `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_yaw_rotation_degradation_claude/`): does jointly rotating the panorama and the source/reference coordinates in yaw substantially degrade synthesis? Evaluator `eval_yaw_rotation.py` (hashed reference manifest `ckpt/yaw_rotation/reference_manifest.json`, TF32 off, every batch padded to 16, per-query seeded Griffin-Lim, condition P = alignment pinned at 0°, E = end-to-end), summariser `tools/summarize_yaw.py --mode full` (paired bootstrap, r_k inside resamples, Bonferroni family 18, room-cluster CIs, TOST, convergence check). Result (canonical `ckpt/yaw_rotation/full_stats.json` / `full_summary.txt`, runs `ckpt/yaw_rotation/sweep_{control,cyl,released}`): **H1 not supported** for the same-budget SimpleViT and the released checkpoint; every adjusted upper bound for EDT/C50 at every angle is below +10 % (max +7.6 %). Degradation is small and peaks at diagonal headings (C50 +4–5 % at ±22.5°/±45°, EDT ≤ +3 %, ~0 at 180° and ±5.6°), i.e. distribution shift from axis-aligned training rooms; E = P to 2e-5. The cylindrical model does not degrade less (EDT D = +2.2 % at −45°); its tokens are equivariant (2e-7) but the learned position pool and the absolute-coordinate embeddings shared by both backbones carry the change. Properly paired k = 0 comparison (same references and phases): cyl EDT −4.4 % with query and room intervals both excluding 0, loss −1.5 %, C50 no difference — supersedes exp_01's unpaired numbers. The k = 0 parity gate needed two pre-specified band amendments (v3: per-model reference-draw, phase, TF32 and batch-shape spreads); the cylindrical model's EDT/C50 are ~2.5× more sensitive to which references it gets. Record committed 2026-09-07 (`4131f7d` + bookkeeping `19a04ef`): every number on the page/results.md comes from the canonical JSON (generators `_results_assets/make_results_{html,md}.py` refuse anything else), all 13 runs are bound post hoc by `_results_assets/bind_provenance.py` (immutable sidecars; report `binding_report.json`) and `check_sweep_acceptance.py` recomputes the gate decision from the bound inputs with the producer pinned at `5febf47`; eight Codex review rounds on the Planner tooling ended with the evidence path confirmed sound and auxiliary items (launcher v3 not certified for a clean re-run, renderer corruption edge cases, non-crash-atomic binder) recorded as open in the analysis. Re-running the acceptance check (~1 min) or the binder is safe and idempotent; do not edit sidecars by hand.
CLAUDE.md:93:exp_04 (yaw augmentation, started 2026-09-12, SOP-native, record `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/`, plan v4 + amendments A1–A10 in §11): train the SimpleViT with per-sample active yaw of the whole scene (offsets d ~ U{0..511} from a counter-seeded generator, `tools/yaw_aug.py`, port of FLAC exp_17; audio untouched; alignment on the rotated geometry) and test non-inferiority at k = 0 (H1, +3 %), reduced degradation vs the control at ±22.5°/±45° (H2, C50 primary) and near-invariance (TOST ±2 %), each with five evaluation seeds 42–46 (manifests `ckpt/yaw_aug/reference_manifest_k{8,1}_seed*.json`). **Closure rule:** exp_03's committed record pins 12 files (`eval_yaw_rotation.py`, `eval_unseen.py`, `eval_xRIR_backbone.py`, `model/*.py`, `tools/{yaw_rotation,reference_manifest,per_sample_metrics}.py`, the dataset module, `utils/spec_utils.py`); any later commit touching them fails `tests/test_exp03_record_tools.py`, so new behaviour lives in new modules that import them. Tool chain (all reviewed by Fable subagents, Codex-coded, 785 tests): `train_xRIR_backbone.py --yaw-aug 1 --yaw-aug-seed 0 --yaw-aug-width 512 [--no-save]`; `tools/provenance.py` (hermetic import-derived closures, data inventories, exclusive manifests / atomic completions, revalidate); `tools/exp04_eval.py` (= the frozen evaluator's functions + immutable eval-manifest handshake, `--conditions P`); `tools/exp04_eval_launch.py` (run dir, manifest, tee, finalisation, `--bind-input`, `--gpu`); `tools/exp04_launcher.py` + `tools/exp04_launch.sh` (modes smoke/probe/full/finalize/refuse-test; golden argv in the record's `yaw_aug_xrir_results_assets/`; resource/banner/args guards; `abort.json`, ABORTED renames, 43 h ceiling on `full` attempts, promotion symlink `ckpt/xRIR_simple_yawaug_8_shot/final`); `tools/exp04_profiles.py` (+ runtime-read `yaw_aug_xrir_results_assets/approved_digests.json`, all-null until the second reviewed commit); `tools/paired_compare.py` (profiles H1_K8/H1_K1/H2_K8/TOST_K8, fail-closed admission) and `tools/results_table.py` (TABLE_V1 → canonical JSON → `worklog/worklog_yixun/model_comparison.md`). Status: rung 4 audit 0/12 800 changed delays; the throughput gate (≤ 5 %) needs a clean GPU (co-tenant probe said 23 %, the kernel costs < 0.7 %); the confirmatory ~30 h training is BLOCKED while the user's FLAC exp_13 chain holds both GPUs (from 2026-09-12 15:51, ~5 days) — do not launch `full` or co-tenant without the user's decision. Long Codex/eval jobs: nohup-detached scripts + Monitor (the harness kills background Bash on false low-memory).
